  <styleguide>This is a help desk and web shop application for consumers.

Tone: friendly and informal. Address the user in the informal form (for example "du" in German and Swedish, "sinä" in Finnish, "tu" in French).

Buttons and menu commands: short imperative verbs ("Open", "Close", "Post"). Statuses and labels: adjectives or nouns, never commands.

Terminology: a "ticket" is a support request, never a travel or event ticket. A "queue" is a group of support tickets. A "post" is a reply in a support ticket.

Keep the product and component names in English. Use sentence case, not title case.</styleguide>
  <duplicates differentcontext="dcaMachineTranslate"/>
</project>
